***REMOVED***"summary": "A workshop that explores how your role as a Connector will require you to engage with diverse individuals from a range of backgrounds and cultures",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>QUT Connect is an on-campus and university run volunteering program which provides current students the opportunity to help new students settle into university life and actively contribute to building a vibrant campus community.<\/p><p>This workshop helps students explore how to appropriately interact with others from a range of cultural and life backgrounds. Topics explored in this workshop include:<\/p><ul><li>Engaging appropriately with individuals and groups from diverse cultural and social backgrounds<\/li><li>How your role as a Connector contributes to building a positive university community<\/li><li>Activities and discussions with fellow students<\/li><\/ul><p>This workshop is one of two mandatory sessions for those wanting to become a QUT Connector.<\/p><p>Please note: this is only an introductory workshop to understanding diversity in a range of communities. For those interested, additional workshops and training will be discussed in the session.<\/p><p><strong>Students signing up for this workshop should be aware that our mandatory training for those wishing to volunteer during Welcome Week in Semester 1 will be held on Friday 30 January (all day). Please save this date if you are wishing to volunteer for the upcoming Welcome Week.<\/strong><\/p>",
