***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Interactive tutorial providing hands-on experience in the essential skills to get you started and working.<\/p><p>Classes are taught on Windows for Endnote v21. Prerequisite: EndNote 21 will need to be preinstalled on the computer you're using for participating in this session. Installation information is found <a href=\"https:\/\/qutvirtual4.qut.edu.au\/group\/student\/it-and-printing\/software-and-learning-tools\/endnote\"><span style=\"background-color: rgba(238, 236, 225, 1)\">here<\/span><\/a>.<\/p><p>Learn how to:<\/p><ul> <li>navigate the user interface to get used to the lay-out and basic functionalities<\/li><li>view, sort and search references in a Library<\/li><li>organize and tag references for projects and workflows using Groups<\/li><li>create a Library and set Bibliographic styles<\/li><li>learn how to enter records manually<\/li><li>populate the Library by exporting from a database, the library search and Google Scholar<\/li><li>download PDF attachments to the references using 'Find Full Text'<\/li><li>use the PDF viewer to add highlights, underlines, strikethoughs and comments<\/li><li>insert citations and format a bibliography in a Word document<\/li><li>edit citations and safely edit Word document text by un-formatting and reformatting<\/li><li>backup libraries safely.<\/li><\/ul><p style=\"text-align: right\">GRE+D DL LIBOSC001<\/p><p style=\"text-align: right\"><\/p>",
