***REMOVED***"summary": "Brisbane\u2019s \u201cbrown snake\u201d isn\u2019t venomous\u2026 it\u2019s not even a real snake! This is the name Brisbanites affectionately give to the Brisbane River. Join this free walking tour and be guided by experienced students to discover more of Brisbane\u2019s unique slang and South Bank sights including the beach!",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Brisbane\u2019s \u201cbrown snake\u201d isn\u2019t venomous\u2026 it\u2019s not even a real snake! This is the name Brisbanites affectionately give to the Brisbane River. Discover more of Brisbane\u2019s unique slang while taking in the brown snake sights.<\/p><p>Walk over the river on one of our many bridges. Welcome to South Bank, where you\u2019ll explore the hustle and bustle of Brisbane\u2019s cultural precinct. <span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)\">Find out about what to do in South Bank, popular food and drink destinatio<\/span>ns in the area and cheap deals from your experienced student guides.<\/p><p>This is a free walking tour departing from QUT Gardens Point campus for a fully guided tour around South Bank before returning to campus. <\/p><p>Remember to wear comfortable clothing, a hat and walking shoes; use sunscreen; and bring a water bottle.&nbsp;<\/p><p>You must register for this session. Tour guides will monitor numbers as registrations are limited based on ideal group size.&nbsp;<\/p><p>Tours will last for 60-90 minutes and will depart from the East Lawn (between P Block and Y Block).<\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">Tour2025.1<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">\"admin_code:early_engagement\"<\/span><\/p>",
