***REMOVED***"summary": "This workshop aims to help Engineering\/Science\/Health students understand how to convert between various units.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Understanding and converting between units of measurement is required for many engineering, medical, and scientific disciplines. This workshop will equip you with the knowledge and skills required to handle various different units and to convert between them.<\/p><p>By the end of this workshop, students will be able to:<\/p><ul> <li>Identify SI units and understand prefixes (such as kilo- and milli-)<\/li><li>Understand common non-SI units and how they are used<\/li><li>Convert units of length, area, volume, and concentration\/density<\/li><\/ul><p>Part of the STEM Academic Preparedness Workshop Program.<\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\"><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">Study Advantage:&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">Confidently Convert Scientific Units<\/span><\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">ADVSSG0167STEMHLS<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">ADVSSG0167STEMENG<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">ADVSSG0167STEMITMPS<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\"><\/span><\/p>",
