***REMOVED***"summary": "A workshop for HDR students and staff to learn more about accessing secondary datasets. ",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>An interactive session to introduce you to secondary datasets, the benefits of reusing data, and how to find and use existing data. <\/p><p>The session will include introductions to:<\/p><ul><li>Data citation<\/li><li>Benefits of reusing data<\/li><li>Considerations to be mindful of when locating and using secondary datasets for research <\/li><li>Datasets available for request, including the Australian Government Data Catalogue (coming soon)<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>More information<\/strong>: <\/p><p>Also known as existing or third-party datasets, secondary datasets are those that a researcher has not collected or created themselves. This type of data can encompass an enormous range of highly original and extensive studies, including rare, unusual and large datasets.  While many datasets are free to access, some are available through a request or application process, and others may require payment.<\/p><p style=\"text-align: right\">LIBOSC004<\/p><strong><\/strong><strong><\/strong>",
