***REMOVED***"summary": "Are you aged 21 or over and returning to study in 2026? Learn practical strategies to help you build resilience, manage stress and maintain a healthy work, life and study balance.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>You'll hear from QUT staff and other mature aged students who will share tips about how to approach study, what support is available and who to ask for help. You'll also have the opportunity to ask questions about what it's like to study as a mature-aged student. <\/p><p>The topics covered will include:<\/p><p>Accommodation \u2013 a student\u2019s perspective of the types of accommodation, options available and the services that can help you.<\/p><p>Transport \u2013 tips for navigating your way around Brisbane via public transport, using cabs and the free inter-campus shuttle bus.<\/p><p>Employment \u2013 about 70% of current QUT students work while studying. Tips will be provided about how to find work. Information about Careers services and support at QUT.<\/p><p>Personal safety \u2013 staying safe while on-campus or out and about around Brisbane.<\/p><p>Learning support \u2013 learn more about how to study, research and write effectively via QUT\u2019s mentoring programs, guides, real-time classes and online tutorials.<\/p><p>Orientation \u2013 tips for what to attend or get involved in and the key dates in Semester 1 to be aware of.<\/p><p>Financial support \u2013 hear about the variety of scholarships, bursaries, emergency loans, free services and other support offered.<\/p><p>Social opportunities \u2013 what\u2019s available and how to get involved.<span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\"><\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">\u201cnon-schoolleaver_2025.2\u201d<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">\"MatureAgedStudentSession2025.2\"<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\"><\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">\"admin_code:early_engagement\"<\/span><\/p>",
