***REMOVED***"summary": "Join us for an interactive look at how to effectively learn in the health sciences",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>There are so many different learning strategies we can use in our studies, but how do they work and which should we use? In this workshop, we take a look at our working memory, and explore how we can apply some evidence based learning strategies to improve our memory and understanding.<\/p><p>By the end of the workshop, students will:<\/p><ul><li>Explore the process of memory formation<\/li><li>Investigate evidence-based learning strategies including dual processing, retrieval practice, spaced&nbsp;repetition,&nbsp;constructive learning and others.<\/li><li>Learn how to identify strategies that work for you and different content to plan and prepare for learning in labs, workshops and personal study<\/li><li>Develop skills to design and build effective learning resources<\/li><\/ul><p>Part of the <em><a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events?page=1&amp;studentSiteId=1&amp;text=SRH2025.1\">Semester Ready: Health program<\/a><\/em>. See the full list <a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events?page=1&amp;studentSiteId=1&amp;text=SRH2025.1\">here<\/a>. <\/p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events?filterId=722&amp;page=1&amp;studentSiteId=1&amp;text=SRH2025.1\"><\/a><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\"><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">SRH2025.1&nbsp;ADVSSG0051a&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMABE&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMBUS&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMCI&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMEDU&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMENG&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMHLS&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMIT&nbsp;ADVSSG0167STEMMPS<\/span><\/span><\/p>",
