***REMOVED***"summary": "Find the information and resources you need to get the most out of your research degree. Zoom link: https:\/\/qut.zoom.us\/j\/84047799435?pwd=QgNnqMaEfTKYJnATAiNNvWMQ8NpGZX.1",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Find the information and resources you need to get the most out of your research degree. This information session will help inform you about your course, the support you can access and exciting opportunities to broaden your skills. HDR Orientation is necessary for all HDR students commencing this year.<\/p><p>This is a hybrid event. We invite you to come to this LIVE HDR Orientation in&nbsp;GP-P421&nbsp;(10:00am to 12:00pm). Also, stay for free lunch and a chance to meet your student support and graduate researcher training teams:12:00pm to 1:00pm. If you are unable to come to campus, there is an option to join via Zoom.&nbsp;<\/p><p><strong style=\"background-color: initial\"><em>What you'll learn:<\/em><\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Understand the requirements of an HDR student at QUT, including timelines and milestones<\/li><li>Get to know various service providers who can offer training and support<\/li><li>Learn how to make the most of your HDR candidature<\/li><li>Plan ways to engage with industry and broader learning during your degree<\/li><\/ul><p><strong><em>Key Benefits:<\/em><\/strong><\/p><ul><li>A research degree at QUT gives you countless opportunities to learn, engage, and develop your skills while you study.&nbsp;<\/li><li>Orientation will help you navigate these opportunities so you can take advantage of everything on offer at QUT.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>What other participants have said:<\/strong><\/p><p><em>'This session is critical in terms of understanding what is required from us and the various resources that are available in reaching those targets easily, while maintaining our health and wellbeing'<\/em><\/p><p>Offering: GRE+D RP RSCH010<\/p>",
