***REMOVED***"name": "QUT Law Lift-Off: launching your future in Law",
***REMOVED***"eventType": "Orientation",
***REMOVED***"eventTypeId": 30,
***REMOVED***"prerequisiteFormId": null,
***REMOVED***"start": "2026-02-20T09:00:00+10:00",
***REMOVED***"end": "2026-02-20T16:00:00+10:00",
***REMOVED***"publish": "2025-12-04T14:28:00+10:00",
***REMOVED***"expire": "2026-02-20T16:00:00+10:00",
***REMOVED***"isActive": true,
***REMOVED***"isCancelled": false,
***REMOVED***"summary": "This one-day program is highly recommended for students commencing the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) in Semester 1 2026",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Welcome to Law at QUT! You have made an exciting decision for your future.&nbsp;<\/p><p><em>Please note<\/em>:&nbsp;there is a separate, <strong>compulsory online 'Law&nbsp;Orientation' package<\/strong> to complete via the MyLLB Canvas site. Further instructions regarding this&nbsp;will be distributed in late January.<\/p><p>In addition, this <strong>Law Lift-Off <\/strong>is an 'optional' event for those able to come on to campus. It will allow you to meet some of your staff and peers, and participate in workshops covering:<\/p><ul><li>Law as a service industry: the importance of developing***REMOVED***  legal skills;<\/li><li>Introduction to the Law Library;<\/li><li>Support available from Careers Educators;<\/li><li>The contribution of law student clubs to your degree;<\/li><li>A Q&amp;A panel discussion, involving current QUT law***REMOVED***  students, staff and alumni.<\/li><\/ul><p>Please don't stress if you are unable to attend on this day, as some of the workshops will be replicated separately throughout the semester, including via online modes.<\/p><p>The day will primarily be delivered as an <strong>on-campus<\/strong> activity.&nbsp;Because numbers are limited, please only register for this event if you intend on coming and staying for the whole program.&nbsp;However, the Q&amp;A&nbsp;panel session (2:30pm-3:30 AEST) will also be offered online via Zoom \u2013 if you just want to join that online, you can do so&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/qut.zoom.us\/j\/84657221671?pwd=XKXKk1LHDxcCJZH3EzNKJEkcbDHo9C.1\" target=\"_blank\">by clicking here <\/a>on the day (without the need to register for the event). This link will also be available on the MyLLB Canvas site, if you need to access it again.<\/p><p><strong>Logistics:<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Please endeavour to arrive on time.<\/li><li>Morning tea and lunch will be provided. If you have specific dietary requirements (eg vegan, GF), please&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/forms.office.com\/Pages\/ResponsePage.aspx?id=o1IL3MVo90SIHZOD2IULlih0cdURfkpCvJxoqZSRc-5URDBDSExWUkY1SUtOQVhCWEpLVklYUDREQi4u\" target=\"_blank\">CLICK HERE<\/a>. Whilst every***REMOVED***  effort will be made to cater for such needs, if you have detailed requirements,***REMOVED***  you may prefer to bring your own lunch or purchase from the retailers on***REMOVED***  campus.<\/li><li>Bring a&nbsp;water bottle (there's chilled taps on campus to***REMOVED***  refill).<\/li><li>Bring something to take notes with: pen &amp; paper,&nbsp;or&nbsp;a&nbsp;laptop.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Questions <\/strong>can be directed to <a href=\"mailto:myllb@qut.edu.au\">myllb@qut.edu.au<\/a> .<\/p><p><strong>QUT Connect:<\/strong><\/p><p>You are also encouraged to register for a QUT Connect session which is run by volunteer students providing commencing students a \"101\" of all things QUT, including support services, IT, and the student experience outside the classroom. If you are a double degree student attending a session on campus, you will most likely be attending a Connect session as part of that orientation program. If you are a single Law student, you may wish to register for the <a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events?filterId=2498\">on-campus Law Connect<\/a> running on <strong>Wednesday 18 February<\/strong>. Details about these QUT Connect events can be found on the <a href=\"https:\/\/qutvirtual4.qut.edu.au\/group\/student\/orientation\/your-orientation\">your orientation<\/a> webpage. This will also provide you the opportunity to explore relevant clubs and societies, including Law societies, at the <a href=\"https:\/\/qutvirtual4.qut.edu.au\/group\/student\/student-life\/events\/welcome-week\">Clubs on Campus<\/a> event.<\/p>",
