***REMOVED***"summary": "Learn Python from the ground up\u2014set up your environment and editor, understand core programming concepts, solve practical activities, and build your own interactive, visual program. You\u2019ll leave confident to design and develop your own small beginner projects, and know where to find future learning, support, and collaborators at QUT.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Learn Python from the ground up\u2014set up your environment and editor, understand core programming concepts, solve practical activities, and build your own interactive, visual program. You\u2019ll leave confident to design and develop your own small beginner projects, and know where to find future learning, support, and collaborators at QUT.<\/p><p><strong>What you\u2019ll learn<\/strong><\/p><ul> <li><strong>Understand key Python concepts:<\/strong> variables, loops, data types, functions, and basic data structures.<\/li><li><strong>Set up your environment &amp; editor:<\/strong> install Python, choose an editor (e.g., IDLE, VS Code) and begin programming confidently.<\/li><li><strong>Solve hands\u2011on activities:<\/strong> short, scaffolded exercises that build from fundamentals to practical problem\u2011solving.<\/li><li><strong>Build your own interactive &amp; visual program:<\/strong> step\u2011by\u2011step guidance to create a simple game that exemplifies foundational Python concepts with inputs, logic, and simple visuals.<\/li><li><strong>Find future learning, support &amp; collaborators:<\/strong> QUT resources, communities, and pathways to keep progressing.<\/li><\/ul><p><br>  <strong>Who should attend:<\/strong> Beginners and refreshers across all disciplines. These sessions are particularly relevant for those new to Python and studying <strong>IFB104, CAB320, and IFN581<\/strong>.<\/p><p><strong>Bring:<\/strong> your device and QUT login.<\/p><p><strong>This session cannot be recorded due to QUT student involvement.<\/strong><\/p><p style=\"text-align: right\"><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">Student Success: Foundations of Python Programming<\/span><\/p>",
