***REMOVED***"summary": "Learn about the Australian job market to succeed in your research career.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Learn some key strategies for landing jobs in Australia. In this workshop, find out about the differences in looking and applying for work in Australia as an HDR student or early career researcher, how to get started and what you need to know before you start. Gain an understanding of finding casual, part-time and research work in Australia, why you need Australian referees, and what Australian employers are expecting from you.<\/p><p><strong>What you'll learn:<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Discover where to find advertised roles<\/li><li>Learn what to do in job applications and interviews<\/li><li>Learn how to build connections and referees<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Key benefits:<\/strong><\/p><ul> <li>Australia has some differences and quirks compared to other countries in terms of how its job market works and how you should work within it. This workshop will reveal some of these important factors.<\/li><li>Fast-track your way to be job-ready.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>What previous participants have said:<\/strong><\/p><p><em>I love Karen's enthusiasm when explaining the materials. She also set the fact that for internationals, it will be harder for us, but she also gives practical suggestion that we can use immediately.<\/em><\/p><p>Offering: GRE+D CD RSCH200<\/p>",
