***REMOVED***"summary": "This workshop demystifies GenAI and shows you, step by step, how to use QUT\u2011provided tools safely, effectively, and ethically. We\u2019ll use short demos and guided hands\u2011on practice with practical examples. We\u2019ll provide you with a quick\u2011start prompt cheat sheet, a reliability checklist, and links to QUT support resources.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>This workshop demystifies GenAI and shows you, step by step, how to use QUT\u2011provided tools safely, effectively, and ethically. We\u2019ll use short demos and guided hands\u2011on practice with practical examples. We\u2019ll provide you with a quick\u2011start prompt cheat sheet, a reliability checklist, and links to QUT support resources.<br> <strong>What you\u2019ll learn<\/strong><\/p><ul> <li><strong>Use QUT\u2011provided GenAI with confidence:<\/strong> where to find it, how it fits into your study, and smart ways to integrate it into your own ways of working and experimenting.<\/li><li><strong>Understand what GenAI can (and can\u2019t) do:<\/strong> strengths for brainstorming, drafting, explanation, coding assistance and study planning and the limitations to keep in mind.<\/li><li><strong>Prompting tricks &amp; shortcuts:<\/strong> role prompts, structured templates, iteration, \u201cshow\u2011your\u2011work\u201d prompts, and quick strategies for summarising, transforming and verifying information.<\/li><li><strong>Academic integrity with GenAI:<\/strong> In alignment with QUT policy when and how to disclose use and keeping your own understanding front and centre.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Who should attend:<\/strong> If you\u2019re new to GenAI or keen to sharpen skills. Open to all QUT students and relevant to all disciplines.<\/p><p><strong>Bring:<\/strong> Your device and QUT login.<\/p><p><strong>This session cannot be recorded due to QUT student involvement.<\/strong><\/p><p style=\"text-align: right\">ADVSSG0107<\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)\">Student Success: Foundations of Python Programming<\/span><\/p>",
