***REMOVED***"summary": "Gain an overview of the essential strategies for effective HDR supervision",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Gain an overview of the essential strategies for effective HDR supervision. This 2-week moderated online module provides you with foundational instruction on your responsibilities as a supervisor, advice and tips on supervisory practice, and case studies and scenarios to highlight how you may implement key strategies. Participation may take about two hours per week, involving engaging in online content and discussing supervisory issues with a community of peers and an experienced supervisor in an online forum. This course must be completed within six months of starting a first supervision by all QUT supervisors (excluding experienced supervisors new to QUT) and is offered twice a year. Experienced supervisors may also undertake this module if they wish to do so for their professional development.<\/p><p><strong>What you'll learn:<\/strong><\/p><ul> \n<li>Explore the complexities and responsibilities of the role of the HDR supervisor<\/li><li>Develop strategies for working effectively with your students and other supervisors<\/li><li>Understand ways of supporting and guiding your students<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Key benefits:<\/strong><\/p><ul> \n<li>Get the most out of your students and yourself as a supervisor<\/li><li>Completing this course satisfies QUT Supervisor accreditation requirements for two years<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>What previous participants have said:<\/strong><\/p><p><em><strong><\/strong>It is very well structured, practical, and its online format provides flexibility\u2026 Very pleased I enrolled! Highly recommend this course!<\/em><\/p><p>Offering: GRE+D SUP RSCS011<\/p>",
