***REMOVED***"summary": "Want to feel more organised, confident, and connected this semester? Make\u2011it Monday is your weekly drop\u2011in to build practical uni skills without the pressure.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<h3>\u2b50 Why You Should Join Make\u2011it Monday \u2b50<\/h3><p>Want to feel more organised, confident, and connected this semester? <strong>Make\u2011it Monday<\/strong> is your weekly drop\u2011in to build practical uni skills <em>without the pressure<\/em>.<\/p><p>Here\u2019s why students love it:<br>\u2728 <strong>It actually helps.<\/strong> Each activity gives you something useful \u2014 a study plan, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 starter, flashcards, or even a mindful origami break to reset your brain.<\/p><p>\u2728 <strong>You don\u2019t need to know anything before you walk in.<\/strong> We guide you through the activity step\u2011by\u2011step, answer your questions, and help you find the right resources.<\/p><p>\u2728 <strong>It\u2019s flexible and stress\u2011free.<\/strong> Drop in any time, stay as long as you want, and join a welcoming space designed to make uni feel less overwhelming.<\/p><p>\u2728 <strong>You\u2019ll walk away with real tools that make a difference.<\/strong> Templates, examples, tips, and resources are all ready to go each week.<\/p><p>Start your week with something easy, practical, and good for your study life. Come say hi, have a cup of tea or a hot chocolate, grab a snack&nbsp;and make something that\u2019ll set you up for success. \ud83d\udc9b\ud83d\udcd8<\/p><p><strong>Welcome Week - Origami<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Weeks 1 and 2 - Study Planning<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Weeks 3 and 4 - Resumes<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Weeks 5 and 6 - Flashcards<\/strong><\/p>",
