***REMOVED***"summary": "Break down academic assessment tasks with confidence - learn how to interpret instructions, manage workloads, and plan your approach to postgraduate assignments in Health",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Understanding exactly what is required in your assessments is key to academic success. This interactive workshop will guide you through breaking down complex assignment instructions for essays, research projects, and case studies. You'll develop strategies to plan and manage larger, high-stakes tasks with confidence -&nbsp;mapping out timelines for research, drafting, and revision.<\/p><p>You\u2019ll also gain practical tips for efficient and critical reading techniques to help you navigate postgraduate workloads more effectively.<\/p><p>Activities include hands-on task analysis of sample assessments, peer discussions to compare approaches and strategies, and tools for structuring and managing longer assignments<\/p><p>Part of the <em style=\"background-color: initial\"><a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events?page=1&amp;studentSiteId=1&amp;text=SRH2025.1\">Semester Ready Health Program<\/a><\/em>. See the full list <a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events?page=1&amp;studentSiteId=1&amp;text=SRH2025.1\">here<\/a>.&nbsp;<\/p><p><span style=\"font-size: 10px\">SRH2025.1.&nbsp;<\/span><\/p><p style=\"text-align: right\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px\">ADVSSG0071<\/span><\/p>",
