***REMOVED***"summary": "HPC Basics - Intro to the HPC - March 2026",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>\n\t<strong><span style=\"color: rgba(31, 73, 125, 1)\">How it works<\/span><br>\n\t<\/strong>The HPC Basics training is made up of two sessions:&nbsp;<\/p>\n<table class=\"table table-bordered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n\t<td>\n\t\t<strong>Session<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Date\/Time<\/strong><strong><\/strong><\/td>\n\t<td>\n\t\t<strong>Register<\/strong>\n\t<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n\t<td>\n\t\t1&nbsp;Intro to the Unix shell\n\t<\/td>\n\t<td>Mon 2 March, 9.30m-12.30pm<br>\n\t<\/td>\n\t<td><a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events\/detail\/6857024\">Book here<\/a><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n\t<td>\n\t\t2&nbsp;Intro to the HPC Aqua<br>(High Performance Computer)\n\t<\/td>\n\t<td>Tues 3 March, 9.30am-12.30pm\n\t<\/td>\n\t<td>\n\t\tSelect the BOOK button above\n\t<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table><p>\n\tThese sessions are delivered online and are designed for HDR students and Staff at QUT who need to learn how to use the HPC (Aqua) or refresh their knowledge.<\/p><p>\n\t<strong><span style=\"color: rgba(31, 73, 125, 1)\">Benefits<br>\n\t<\/span><\/strong><span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)\">Researchers attending both sessions will become familiar with the Unix shell and learn how to log on to QUT\u2019s new HPC Aqua to copy files, edit scripts and submit jobs. These sessions are introductory only.<\/span><\/p><p>\n\t<strong><span style=\"color: rgba(31, 73, 125, 1)\">How to book<\/span><\/strong><br>\n\t<span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)\"><\/span><span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)\">NOTE: this event is for the <em style=\"background-color: initial\">Session 2: Intro to the HPC.<br>\n\t<\/em><\/span>To book into session 1 please see link in table above.<\/p><p>\n\t<strong><span style=\"\"><span style=\"color: rgba(192, 80, 77, 1); font-size: 16px\">HPC account required<\/span><\/span><br>\n\t<\/strong>Please ensure you have a HPC account before the second session <em>Intro to the HPC<\/em>. If you don't have a HPC account, you won't be able to participate in the session.<br>\n\tIf you don't have a HPC account, you can request one&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/heat2.qut.edu.au\/HEAT\/Login.aspx?ProviderName=QUT+SAML&amp;Role=SelfService&amp;Scope=SelfServiceMobile&amp;CommandId=NewServiceRequestByOfferingId&amp;Tab=ServiceCatalog&amp;Template=F86AFEC39A8C454A890E989D24914A8E\">here<\/a>.<\/p>",
