***REMOVED***"summary": "If you are working with data, Excel can be an excellent tool for understanding, visualising, and even preparing data for use in other workflows. This workshop seeks to give you basic tools for data exploration and processing.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>This workshop introduces Excel as a data exploration, preparation, and analysis tool. It will help you develop and apply formulas, text manipulation, grouping through pivot tables, visualisations, cleaning data, and more. It won\u2019t make you an expert in data analysis, but it\u2019s a great place to start if you will be working with data in your course.&nbsp;<\/p><p>This workshop assumes basic knowledge of Excel, including opening files and modifying cells, but assumes you are new to working with data operations. If you are new to Excel, we recommend attending&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/unihub.qut.edu.au\/students\/events?page=1&amp;studentSiteId=1&amp;text=getting%20started%20with%20excel\">Getting Started with Excel workshop<\/a> first.<\/p><p>Please note, this is a general Excel workshop aimed at students in all courses.<\/p><p>\n\tPlease <strong>bring your own laptop<\/strong> to work on, or <a href=\"https:\/\/qutvirtual4.qut.edu.au\/group\/student\/it-and-printing\/computer-labs-and-loans\">borrow one<\/a> as a short term loan from HiQ.<\/p><p>Part of the STEM Academic Preparedness Workshop Program<\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)\"><br><\/span><\/p><p style=\"text-align: right\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px\"><span style=\"color: rgba(216, 216, 216, 1)\">ADVSSG0167STEMABE<br>ADVSSG0167STEMBUS<br>ADVSSG0167STEMCI<br>ADVSSG0167STEMEDU<br>ADVSSG0167STEMENG<br>ADVSSG0167STEMHLS<br>ADVSSG0167STEMITMPS<\/span><\/span><\/p>",
