***REMOVED***"summary": "Improve your understanding of Undergraduate Nursing assignments to identify task requirements and prepare more effectively. Get support with writing, referencing, and understanding AI requirements, as well as building English language skills including communication and grammar. ",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>In Nursing COMPASS (Collaborative Mentoring with Peer-Assisted Support for Success)&nbsp;drop-in sessions you will have the opportunity to ask questions in small groups&nbsp;about your assessments in Nursing units. The trained and knowledgeable&nbsp;Peer Learning Facilitators, with valuable experience in nursing units, will help you to:<\/p><ul><li>Develop your skills in understanding task expectations.<\/li><li>Listen to how other students frame their questions and find ways to overcome challenges.<\/li><li>Build strategies and confidence for researching and writing your responses.<\/li><li>Develop your confidence and ability in checking that your work meets the assessment's expectations through interaction with the task sheet and rubric.&nbsp;<\/li><\/ul><p>The sessions are also a great opportunity to:<\/p><ul><li>Connect with students in your course.<\/li><li>Get feedback and support with writing and English grammar.<\/li><\/ul><p>The sessions are open to any students in&nbsp;NS42 Bachelor of Nursing or NS89 Master of Nursing Entry to Practice.<\/p><p>ADVSSG0022<\/p>",
