***REMOVED***"summary": "The module Approaches to Planning and Designing Learning is an opportunity for professional development for those who teach or support learning. This facilitated workshop complements the online self-directed learning available on Canvas.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>This workshop forms part of the Foundational Learning module Approaches to Planning and Designing Learning. The workshop complements the online self-directed component available <u style=\"background-color: initial\"><a href=\"https:\/\/bit.ly\/FL1_Register\">via Canvas<\/a><\/u>.<\/p><p>On completion of the module you will be able to:<\/p><ul> <li>Apply constructive alignment of aims, teaching and learning, and assessment to your teaching.<\/li><li>Apply curriculum design principles.<\/li><li>Review evidence informed approaches to planning and design of learning and teaching.<\/li><\/ul><p>A certificate of completion will be issued once you have completed the online component and attended the facilitated workshop associated with this module.<\/p><p>Professional Development in Learning and Teaching (PDLT) is available to all academic, sessional and professional staff at QUT who teach or support learning. The broad suite of modules are designed to enable you to access evidence-based development in line with your teaching needs and professional development.<\/p><p>This module is part of the Foundational Learning set for those who are new to learning and teaching or are interested in reviewing core concepts and models to develop effective educational practice. This module will support your development as an educator and help you produce a reflective profile that will enable you to apply for Higher Education Academy (HEA) Fellowship.<\/p>",
