***REMOVED***"summary": "The module Enabling Support for Students is an opportunity for professional development for those who teach or support learning. This interactive facilitated workshop complements the self-directed learning available on Canvas.",
***REMOVED***"details": "<p>\n\tThis interactive workshop forms part of the Foundational Learning module Enabling Support for Students. The interactive workshop complements the online self-directed component available&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/bit.ly\/FL7_Register\">via Canvas<\/a>.<\/p><p>\n\tOn completion of the module you will be able to:<\/p><ul>\n\t\n<li>Discuss key factors affecting access and equity in higher education.<\/li><li>Evaluate principles of transition pedagogy and hidden curriculum.<\/li><li>Design a strategy for supporting students in your disciplinary context.<\/li><\/ul><p>\n\tA certificate of completion will be issued once you have completed the online component and attended the facilitated workshop associated with this module.<\/p><p>\n\tProfessional Development in Learning and Teaching (PDLT) is available to all academic, sessional and professional staff at QUT who teach or support learning. The broad suite of modules are designed to enable you to access evidence-based development in line with your teaching needs and professional development.<\/p><p>\n\tThis module is part of the Foundational Learning set for those who are new to learning and teaching or are interested in reviewing core concepts and models to develop effective educational practice. This module will support your development as an educator and help you produce a reflective profile that will enable you to apply for Higher Education Academy (HEA) Fellowship.<\/p>",
